Jambavan rebukes silent aloof Hanuman --- Declares Hanuman equal to Sugriva, Rama and Lakshmana --- Compares Hanuman strength to Garuda pinions --- Recounts Anjana transformation and union with Wind --- Wind promises a strong wise son to Anjana --- Infant Hanuman leaps toward sun and suffers Indra thunderbolt --- Gains name Hanuman from broken jaw --- Gods grant weapon-proof life and death at will --- Jambavan recalls circling earth and gathering life herbs --- Urges Hanuman to rise and leap ocean like Vishnu